# Draft knowledge entry: open62541 raw Ethernet CMake capability boundary

id: DRAFT-open62541-ohos-musl-posix-ethernet-1.5.6
trigger_tool: cc|clang|ld|cmake|conan
phase: compilation|linking
error_signature: redefinition of 'sockaddr_storage'|undefined symbol: UA_ConnectionManager_new_POSIX_Ethernet
severity: 2
category: compat|musl|network|linking|open62541
match_keywords: open62541, eventloop_posix_eth.c, ua_config_default.c, POSIX_Ethernet, sockaddr_storage, linux/socket.h, OHOS
title: open62541 raw Ethernet source and registration must share the same CMake capability
root_cause: >
  The raw Ethernet source includes Linux kernel networking headers that conflict
  with the OHOS musl socket headers. The implementation and its default
  registration must use the same build capability or the registration can
  reference UA_ConnectionManager_new_POSIX_Ethernet after the implementation is
  excluded, producing a link-time undefined symbol.
affected_scope: >
  open62541 builds using the default POSIX plugin configuration on the OHOS SDK.
  The pattern also applies when a platform condition excludes a plugin
  implementation but leaves default registration enabled.
verification_cmd: >
  conan create archives/o/open62541/1.5.6 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64
  -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=missing;
  run the consumer on the OHOS shadow device and require no POSIX_Ethernet
  undefined-symbol failure.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: paired-cmake-capability-option
rec_description: >
  Add UA_ENABLE_POSIX_ETHERNET as a CMake option defaulting to ON. Set it OFF
  from the Conan OHOS configuration when the sysroot lacks Linux raw-socket
  headers, exclude eventloop_posix_eth.c from plugin_sources, and define the
  same capability for open62541-plugins only when enabled. Use that generic
  capability definition for the matching default registration. Preserve the
  normal TCP/UDP POSIX event loop and do not add a fake implementation.
rec_command: >
  Apply patches/0002-cmake-posix-ethernet-option.patch and
  0003-plugins-ua_config_default.c.patch, set
  UA_ENABLE_POSIX_ETHERNET=OFF for the OHOS Conan build, then rebuild and link
  the consumer.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: open62541-ohos-plugin-capability
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: inspect-plugin-registration
fallback_description: >
  If the symbol remains, inspect both the compiled source list and the default
  plugin registration before changing package libraries or linker flags.
fallback_command: rg -n "POSIX_Ethernet|eventloop_posix_eth" source build
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: plugin-source-registration-audit
forbid_1_pattern: add a fake POSIX_Ethernet implementation to mask the link error
forbid_1_reason: The underlying Linux kernel header set is incompatible with the OHOS sysroot.
forbid_1_consequence: The package may compile but expose unsupported or unsafe raw Ethernet behavior.
forbid_2_pattern: link extra host Linux networking libraries to resolve the symbol
forbid_2_reason: The failure is a source/registration capability mismatch, not a missing system library.
forbid_2_consequence: Host ABI assumptions leak into the OHOS package and remain non-reproducible.
principles: paired-capability-guards, musl-sysroot-boundary, link-error-root-cause
